                                "text": "Du hast den Backslash vergessen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0b9730b6-32d5-416d-814c-5a3f9f326335",
                        "source_entry_id": "a492963b-8130-33a4-8226-63bbc411cbb4",
                        "source_sense_id": "324fdc68-33ee-30be-af56-467952f7bb1e",
                        "source_sense_description": "EDV: Schrägstrich, der von oben links nach unten rechts verläuft",
                        "target_lang_word": "backslash",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "backslash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eeaf3506-a580-381f-8f86-b47560ae3491",
                                        "entry_id": "58ca01be-e842-358f-94f9-69a74ad863ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The punctuation mark \\\\."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "709e964f-15e4-3e84-876f-5c2165b50589",
                                        "entry_id": "58ca01be-e842-358f-94f9-69a74ad863ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used erroneously in reference to, or in reading out, the ordinary slash, that is, the punctuation mark /."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4998d4d6-1f1d-4b93-bcd3-32dfb37cc898",
                                                "sense_id": "709e964f-15e4-3e84-876f-5c2165b50589",
                                                "text": "[…] I was trying to find a web-site for which I had been given the following address: http://www.isop.ucla.edu/pacrim/pubs/korjournal.htm. […] I began to work backwards, removing first the last part of the address following the last backslash (/korjournal.htm)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77e393f7-9fe8-4c3e-9bc5-204ef7a6b44f",
                                                "sense_id": "709e964f-15e4-3e84-876f-5c2165b50589",
                                                "text": "“So, do what I tell you. Open a browser window and type this in the menu^([sic]) bar: F-T-P colon backslash backslash euronews dot net backslash...”\nI pecked carefully at the keyboard as he dictated a URL that was about fifty characters long, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5665fb50-d75a-4661-b666-bcccb47cd903",
                                                "sense_id": "709e964f-15e4-3e84-876f-5c2165b50589",
                                                "text": "Also, avoid submenus^([sic]) that can confuse the audience—if you're giving lengthy Web site addresses full of backslashes, shorten it so only the Web site's home page is given."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "backslash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc123ce8-f19a-35a6-aec8-015b5fc6f1ba",
                                        "entry_id": "51897f7a-1ebc-38df-8e02-a0977b50d346",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To escape (a metacharacter) by prepending a backslash that serves as an escape character, thereby forming an escape sequence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e8d36cae-7184-4554-8413-5e1b5ee28162",
                        "source_entry_id": "a492963b-8130-33a4-8226-63bbc411cbb4",
                        "source_sense_id": "324fdc68-33ee-30be-af56-467952f7bb1e",
                        "source_sense_description": "EDV: Schrägstrich, der von oben links nach unten rechts verläuft",
                        "target_lang_word": "antislash",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "antislash",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95f24c8c-d808-3127-9d72-e9aa68882741",
                                        "entry_id": "84865b54-c025-356e-aae4-1353a3f8754c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Barre oblique inverse : \\\\."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Anglicism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94bfb415-5a30-41a9-a4c3-e3a12154858c",
                                                "sense_id": "95f24c8c-d808-3127-9d72-e9aa68882741",
                                                "text": "Vous remarquez qu’il n'y a pas besoin de faire précéder les accolades avec le caractère antislash."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31303771-e5e1-4584-a6dc-5f3c8e40154f",
                                                "sense_id": "95f24c8c-d808-3127-9d72-e9aa68882741",
                                                "text": "Pour des questions de lisibilité et d'homogénéité d'écriture, il est préférable d'éviter les combinaisons de simples quotes et antislash dans une même expression si cela n'est pas indispensable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
